2. Component-specific terms
---------------------------

The following paths have explicit upstream license or provenance notices:

* `src/seg/models_deep_seg.py` is licensed under GNU GPL version 3, as stated
  in its file header by Jonathan Vacher. The header does not state an
  "or later" option. See https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.en.html.

* `src/toolbox.py` and `src/toolbox_deep.py` are licensed under Creative
  Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), as stated in their file headers by Jonathan Vacher.
  See https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/.

* `src/seg/gmm_prior.py` and `src/seg/smm_prior.py` state that they reuse code
  and comments from `sklearn.mixture.gmm` and identify modifications by
  Jonathan Vacher and Luis Carlos Garcia-Peraza Herrera. The reused
  scikit-learn material remains under scikit-learn's BSD 3-Clause License.
  Preserve the applicable upstream copyright notice, BSD conditions, and
  disclaimer, as well as the modification credits in the source files. See
  https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/blob/main/COPYING. The source
  headers do not identify the exact scikit-learn release that was reused, so
  this repository does not supply a version-specific upstream notice.

* The `loadmat_h5` function in `src/import_utils.py` is marked as coming from
  https://github.com/rkp8000/loadmat_h5. That upstream repository has no
  license file; its README invites users to copy and paste the function but
  does not state license terms granting the usual rights to modify and
  redistribute it. The MIT grant above does not cover this function. Do not
  assume rights beyond the upstream statement and applicable law; obtain
  permission from the upstream copyright holder or replace the function if
  broader rights are required.

Other files described as collaborative lab code are not automatically covered
by Linghao Xu's MIT grant. If a file or contribution cannot be clearly
identified as either Linghao Xu's original work or material governed by one of
the notices above, no additional permission is granted by this terms file.

3. Consequences for use and redistribution
------------------------------------------

The CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 components and adaptations of them may be used only for
NonCommercial purposes and remain subject to Attribution and ShareAlike. The
repository as distributed therefore must not be treated as a commercially
usable whole. This does not add a NonCommercial restriction to independent
components under other licenses.

The GNU GPLv3 and CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 components retain separate terms. This file
does not grant permission to relicense the aggregate under either license, or
under any other single unified license. Redistribution must preserve the
source-level notices, this file, and `NOTICE.md`, and must comply with every
applicable component license. If combining components into one derivative
work would impose incompatible obligations, obtain separate permission from
the relevant copyright holders or do not distribute that combined work.

Consult `NOTICE.md` and the source headers before using or redistributing any
part of this repository.
